{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"And Moses and Eleazar the priest did\"</b> — and the princes are not mentioned — is that it is known they fulfilled the command of Moses, who is the authority over them. But concerning the matter of the census it says: \"These are the reckoned ones whom Moses and Aaron and the princes of Israel reckoned\" (Numbers 1:44). And perhaps the reason here is that HaShem commanded that the fathers of the congregation be there because it is a matter of money, so they would not suspect Eleazar of taking more than what was commanded to him, and the command was left to their discretion, and they said, 'Far be it from us, for he is the angel of YHWH,' and there is no need for us to be there."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:50.477682188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}